  (text "NEW for the Commander: IEEE 802.3at (Type 2, class 4) powered device + isolated 5 V flyback,\nreplacing the Radxa ZERO 3E PoE HAT. Built around TI TPS23754 following the datasheet typical\napplication (SLVS885I, section 8.2) in its diode-rectified form (GAT2 unused, DT tied to VB).\n\nEverything on nets POE_* sits on the PRIMARY side of the isolation barrier. The only parts that\nbridge the barrier are T1 (flyback transformer), U31 (optocoupler) and C518 (Y capacitor).\nAUDIT: magnetics, current-sense, clamp and loop-compensation values are first-pass numbers and\nmust be validated on the bench (or replaced by the values of the chosen transformer's reference design)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid "bd79f362-fc60-54d3-a7cd-04abc72756c8"))
